## corpus/comptime/layout_query_repr_c.lu
//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="C3 12 4 0 4 8\nP3 6 1 0 1 5\nGdtr 10 1 0 2\nA16 16 16 0\nOuter 48 16 0 16 32\nPNest 10 2 0 1 8\nPage 4096 4096\nscalars 1 2 8 8 1 8\n")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: abi.layout.query, abi.layout.c, abi.layout.packed, abi.layout.align, comptime.layout
//!
//! kw08 (K4, STATUS #31): `size_of(T)`, `align_of(T)` and
//! `offset_of(T, field)` answer at compile time for every `#[repr(c)]`
//! type, from the clause's layout rather than codegen's. Every number
//! here is what gcc 16.2.1 and clang 23.1.1 print for `sizeof`,
//! `_Alignof` and `offsetof` on the same declarations (kasumi,
//! `c-layouts-kasumi.log`; `repr_c_raw_layout.rs` asks them on every
//! CI host). At trunk eb955c3b `size_of` of a struct was E0708 and
//! `align_of` / `offset_of` did not exist.
## corpus/membrane/extern_let_image.lu
//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="header ok\n")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: abi.link.extern, mem.unsafe.raw.1
//!
//! kw09 (K6, STATUS #31): `extern "c" let NAME: *T` names a symbol the
//! link defines; its value is the symbol's address (`[abi.link.extern]`).
//! Every hosted link defines one at the image's own header — ELF's
//! `__ehdr_start`, Mach-O's `__mh_execute_header`, PE's `__ImageBase` —
//! so each host's declaration is chosen by `cfg(target)` and the program
//! reads the header's first byte through it. The checked machine and
//! lupin model no link and refuse the program by name.
## corpus/memory/packed_fields_at_offset_of.lu
//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="10 0 2\n255 0 0 16 0 0 0 0 0 0\n255 4096\n")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: abi.layout.query, abi.layout.packed, mem.unsafe.raw.1
//!
//! kw08 (K4): a packed struct's fields are scalar raw accesses at
//! `offset_of`, which every machine models — the checked machine too,
//! which refuses a whole-aggregate raw store by name. A GDTR is written
//! byte by byte at its fields' offsets (0 and 2, size 10: the layout
//! `lgdt` reads) and read back the same way. At trunk eb955c3b `packed`
//! was E0817 and `offset_of` did not exist.
## corpus/memory/prov_addr_with_addr.lu
//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="5 11\n")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: mem.prov.expose
//!
//! kw06 (K9(a)): `with_addr` keeps the receiver's provenance — no
//! exposure, no angelic resolution — so the write through `q` is a
//! write into `p`'s allocation at offset 5. The compiled tiers lower it
//! as an offset from `p`. At trunk 8e36bc1a native and release refused
//! the method; lupin 0.1.45 has no `with_addr` (wolf-interp#184).
